- **Azure Active Directory** — Azure Active Directory was renamed Microsoft Entra ID in 2023.
- **tenant** — An Entra ID tenant is a dedicated instance of the directory for your organization — contoso.onmicrosoft.com, for example.
- **Users.** — Inside the tenant live four object types you must be fluent in: Users. Member users (your employees) and guest users (B2B collaborators from other organizations).
- **Groups.** — Groups. Collections of users (and devices) used to assign access once instead of per-person.
- **security groups** — Two flavors that matter: security groups for access control, and Microsoft 365 groups for collaboration (they come with a mailbox, Teams, SharePoint).
- **Administrative units.** — Administrative units. Subdivisions of the directory that let you delegate administration — the European IT team administers European users, for example — without granting tenant-wide admin rights.

