- **Axis 1 — Layer.** — Axis 1 — Layer. Layer 7 balancers understand HTTP(S): URL maps route /api/ to one backend and /static/ to another, host rules split api.example.com from www.example.com, and they terminate TLS.
- **Layer 4** — Layer 4 balancers move TCP/UDP/SSL bytes without inspecting them — faster, dumber, right for non-HTTP protocols (game servers, raw TLS passthrough, databases).
- **Axis 2 — Facing.** — Axis 2 — Facing. External faces the internet.
- **Internal** — Internal faces your VPC — private VIPs for service-to-service traffic (your app tier calling your API tier without ever leaving the network — Module 3's private recipe extended).
- **Axis 3 — Scope.** — Axis 3 — Scope. Global balancers (external HTTP(S), external proxy TCP/SSL) run on the anycast edge — one VIP, worldwide.
- **Regional** — Regional balancers live in one region — for compliance pinning or internal traffic.

