- **The core.** — The core. Most resources bill per second (with a one-minute minimum for VMs) — you pay for what the meter ran.
- **SKU** — Every charge traces to a SKU: a specific resource in a specific region (E2 Instance Core running in Iowa is a different SKU from the same core in Belgium — Module 1's "price varies by region" rule, formalized).
- **provisioned** — Some services bill provisioned (a Filestore share's terabytes, a Spanner node's hours — used or not), others consumed (BigQuery bytes scanned, Cloud Run requests).
- **Lever 1 — Sustained-use discounts.** — Lever 1 — Sustained-use discounts. Automatic, no action: run Compute Engine VMs for a large fraction of the month and Google discounts up to 30%, applied automatically to the bill.
- **Lever 2 — Committed-use discounts (CUDs).** — Lever 2 — Committed-use discounts (CUDs). Commit to 1 or 3 years, save up to 57% over on-demand.
- **resource-based** — Two flavors: resource-based (commit to specific vCPU/RAM in a region — deepest discounts, least flexibility) and flexible / spend-based (commit to a dollar amount of Compute Engine spend — 1-year ~28%, 3-year ~46% — usable across machine types and regions).

