- **Object Storage** — Object Storage stores objects — files plus metadata — in buckets inside a regional namespace (your tenancy's unique storage identifier).
- **Block Volumes** — Block Volumes are virtual disks attached to instances — high-performance, low-latency block I/O.
- **VPUs — volume performance units** — Volumes live in an AD (attachable within it), range from 50 GB to 32 TB, and performance scales with VPUs — volume performance units — which you dial per volume.
- **File Storage (FSS)** — File Storage (FSS) is a shared NFS filesystem — mountable from many instances simultaneously.
- **mount target** — You create a filesystem, an export, and a mount target (an IP in your VCN's subnet), then mount -t nfs from each client.
- **storage tiers** — Object Storage has storage tiers. Standard — immediate access, for hot data.

