- **Virtualization → cloud** — one physical machine becomes many virtual ones; the cloud is renting those slices on demand with an API.
- **IaaS/PaaS/SaaS** — rent the machine (EC2), rent the platform (managed databases), rent the software (Gmail). Responsibility shifts up the stack.
- **Regions & AZs** — regions are geographic areas; availability zones are isolated data centers inside them. Spread workloads across AZs.
- **CapEx vs OpEx** — buying servers (capital expense) vs renting by the hour (operating expense); the cloud converts one to the other.
- **Shared responsibility** — the provider secures *of* the cloud (hardware, hypervisor); you secure *in* the cloud (your data, access, config).

