1. **Skeleton** — fill the ATS-safe one-page template: standard headings, reverse-chronological, no tables-as-layout. 2. **Bullet workshop** — rewrite ten bullets with the impact formula (action verb + what you built + outcome + metric); kill every vague verb ('helped', 'worked on'). 3. **Tailoring pass** — take one real posting, map its keywords to your genuine evidence, and produce a tailored copy — without inventing experience. 4. **The six-second test** — hand the draft to a friend (or Noah): in six seconds, can they name your target role and one proof point? 5. **Noah line-by-line** — submit the draft; Noah flags filler, unverified metrics, and keyword stuffing until every bullet is specific and honest.

