1. **Inputs** — write down your real availability (hours/week), your target start date, and your target role; these are the constraints the plan must respect. 2. **30-60-90 skeleton** — fill the three horizons: calibrate + launch (days 1–30), double down on what's working (31–60), close + negotiate (61–90). 3. **Weekly targets** — set concrete numbers per week: applications, networking touches, skill reps, content posts. 4. **Evolution half** — draft your years 1–3 certification and skills sequence; the job is the start of the trajectory, not the end. 5. **Noah calendar** — hand Noah your availability and target date; Noah generates the personalized AHEP calendar and runs the weekly review (on track / slipped / change the plan).

