- **Entry tier — prove the vocabulary** — AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner, Azure Fundamentals (AZ-900), and Google Cloud Digital Leader each validate the same foundation: cloud concepts, shared responsibility, core services, and pricing basics. Pick one cloud first; the other two come fast once the mental model is built. - **Associate tier — prove the build** — AWS Solutions Architect – Associate, Azure Administrator Associate (AZ-104), and OCI Architect Associate test whether you can design and operate real workloads: resilience, performance, security, cost. These are the hiring-filter exams. - **Professional tier — prove the judgment** — AWS Solutions Architect – Professional assumes the associate baseline and adds complex, multi-account, migration-heavy scenarios. It's a capstone, not an entry ticket: sit it after the associate and real project reps. - **The exam-code rule** — vendor exam codes and formats change; always confirm the current code and exam guide on the vendor's certification site before booking.

