A set is an unordered collection of distinct elements. Union ∪, intersection ∩, complement, difference \. |A| is cardinality. Inclusion–exclusion: |A∪B| = |A|+|B|−|A∩B| — add both, subtract the double-count. Worked example (verified): 120 hosts; 45 run Linux (L), 70 run Windows (W), 25 run both (dual-boot). |L∪W| = 45+70−25 = 90. Hosts running neither: 120−90 = 30. Three-set version adds back the triple intersection: |A∪B∪C| = Σ|A|−Σ|A∩B|+|A∩B∩C|. Venn diagrams are this formula drawn. In monitoring, "alerts from source A or source B" is a union — deduplicate the overlap or you double-count incidents.

